WEBVTT

00:00:07.624 --> 00:00:09.452
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:10.710
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:12.551 --> 00:00:13.187
Mary!

00:00:13.359 --> 00:00:13.981
No!

00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:16.952
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.575
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:21.645 --> 00:00:23.057
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:23.749 --> 00:00:24.883
I can't do this alone.

00:00:27.347 --> 00:00:28.288
No!

00:00:30.903 --> 00:00:32.010
We got work to do.

00:00:32.729 --> 00:00:35.113
This was dad's single
most valuable possession.

00:00:35.181 --> 00:00:37.325
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:37.463 --> 00:00:39.410
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:39.493 --> 00:00:40.766
You know, saving people,

00:00:40.849 --> 00:00:41.873
Hunting things,

00:00:41.928 --> 00:00:42.842
Family business.

00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:43.340
No.

00:00:43.451 --> 00:00:44.767
I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:44.861 --> 00:00:46.285
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:46.344 --> 00:00:47.728
Sam, You know we're gonna find dad,

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:48.162
Right?

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.168
Yeah. I know.

00:01:32.955 --> 00:01:33.748
Nervous flyer?

00:01:34.604 --> 00:01:35.897
It's that obvious, huh?

00:01:37.007 --> 00:01:39.275
You know, what are the odds
of dying in a plane crash?

00:01:39.481 --> 00:01:40.249
I mean, what

00:01:40.418 --> 00:01:41.449
20,000 to one?

00:01:45.309 --> 00:01:45.834
Wow.

00:01:46.584 --> 00:01:48.496
That's, uh, really
reassuring. Thank you.

00:02:14.372 --> 00:02:14.859
Thanks.

00:02:15.646 --> 00:02:16.115
Miranda,

00:02:16.284 --> 00:02:16.921
How are you today?

00:02:17.105 --> 00:02:18.342
I'm doing just fine, Chuck.

00:02:19.954 --> 00:02:21.116
Welcome aboard.

00:02:21.828 --> 00:02:24.583
15c towards the back of
the plane, on the right.

00:02:27.541 --> 00:02:28.759
Have a nice flight, sir.

00:02:31.602 --> 00:02:32.970
Oh, I'm counting on it.

00:02:38.286 --> 00:02:38.942
Um...

00:02:40.741 --> 00:02:42.147
Uh, 11F,

00:02:42.203 --> 00:02:44.115
That's the middle of the
plane, on... Thank you

00:02:46.323 --> 00:02:47.035
...the left.

00:02:59.029 --> 00:02:59.741
Excuse me.

00:03:00.544 --> 00:03:01.819
Do you know how long we've been up?

00:03:01.931 --> 00:03:04.293
Oh, uh... about 40 minutes.

00:03:05.323 --> 00:03:05.886
Wow.

00:03:06.182 --> 00:03:07.550
Time really does fly, huh?

00:03:10.903 --> 00:03:11.615
Excuse me.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.170
I've got to stretch my legs.

00:03:39.832 --> 00:03:41.161
You, what the hell are you doing?!

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.174
Morning, sunshine.

00:04:55.539 --> 00:04:56.307
What time is it?

00:04:56.457 --> 00:04:57.769
Huh, It's about 5:45.

00:04:57.919 --> 00:04:58.631
In the morning?

00:04:58.706 --> 00:04:59.100
Yep.

00:04:59.306 --> 00:05:00.371
Where does the day go?

00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:03.520
Did you get any sleep last night?

00:05:03.726 --> 00:05:05.075
Yeah, I grabbed a couple hours.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:05.788
You, liar

00:05:06.756 --> 00:05:07.881
'Cause I was up at 3:00,

00:05:08.631 --> 00:05:10.430
And you were watching a
George Foreman infomercial.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:11.308
Hey, what can I say?

00:05:11.364 --> 00:05:12.245
It's riveting tv.

00:05:12.676 --> 00:05:14.063
When was the last time you
got a good night's sleep?

00:05:14.307 --> 00:05:14.888
I don't know,

00:05:14.963 --> 00:05:16.553
A little while, I guess.
It's not a big deal

00:05:16.741 --> 00:05:17.471
Yeah, it is.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.364
I appreciate your concern.

00:05:19.402 --> 00:05:20.732
I'm not concerned about you.

00:05:20.751 --> 00:05:23.281
It's your job to keep my ass
alive, so I need you sharp.

00:05:24.698 --> 00:05:26.273
Seriously, are you still
having nightmares about Jess?

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:32.307
Yeah.

00:05:34.085 --> 00:05:35.772
But it's not just her. It's everything.

00:05:36.203 --> 00:05:37.908
I just forgot, you know? This job.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:40.305
Man, it gets to you.

00:05:40.623 --> 00:05:42.629
You can't let it. You can't
bring it home like that.

00:05:43.941 --> 00:05:44.503
So, what?

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:45.103
All this it...

00:05:45.415 --> 00:05:46.446
Never keeps you up at night?

00:05:47.608 --> 00:05:48.076
Never?

00:05:48.432 --> 00:05:49.145
You're never afraid?

00:05:49.426 --> 00:05:50.307
No, not really.

00:05:58.629 --> 00:05:59.413
That's not fear.

00:06:00.725 --> 00:06:01.625
That is precaution.

00:06:02.206 --> 00:06:03.105
All right, whatever.

00:06:03.143 --> 00:06:04.249
I'm too tired to argue.

00:06:13.203 --> 00:06:13.746
Hello?

00:06:14.025 --> 00:06:14.474
Dean,

00:06:14.737 --> 00:06:16.405
It's Jerry Panowski.

00:06:17.386 --> 00:06:19.401
You and your dad helped
me out a couple years back.

00:06:20.485 --> 00:06:21.437
Oh, all right,

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:24.271
Yeah, up in kittanning,
Pennsylvania, the poltergeist thing.

00:06:24.713 --> 00:06:25.643
It's not back, is it?

00:06:25.842 --> 00:06:26.307
No.

00:06:26.684 --> 00:06:27.215
No.

00:06:28.455 --> 00:06:29.274
Thank god, no.

00:06:30.754 --> 00:06:32.503
But it's something else, and...

00:06:33.012 --> 00:06:34.362
Well, I think it could be a lot worse.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:35.558
What is it?

00:06:36.134 --> 00:06:37.148
Can we talk in person?

00:06:42.927 --> 00:06:44.676
Thanks for making the trip so quick.

00:06:44.781 --> 00:06:47.323
I ought to be doing you guys a
favor, not the other way around.

00:06:48.275 --> 00:06:49.780
Dean and your dad really helped me out.

00:06:50.378 --> 00:06:52.016
Yeah, he told me. It was a poltergeist?

00:06:52.083 --> 00:06:52.725
Poltergeist?

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:53.828
Man, I loved that movie.

00:06:53.872 --> 00:06:55.732
Hey, nobody's talking
to you. Keep walking.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.407
Damn right it was a poltergeist
practically tore our house apart.

00:07:00.403 --> 00:07:01.355
Tell you something

00:07:01.993 --> 00:07:03.299
If it wasn't for you and your dad,

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:04.561
I probably wouldn't be alive.

00:07:06.761 --> 00:07:08.533
Your dad said you were off
at college. Is that right?

00:07:09.152 --> 00:07:10.370
Yeah, I was. I'm...

00:07:10.658 --> 00:07:11.787
Taking some time off.

00:07:12.075 --> 00:07:13.669
Well, he was real proud
of you. I could tell.

00:07:14.112 --> 00:07:15.462
He talked about you all the time.

00:07:16.831 --> 00:07:17.451
He did?

00:07:17.827 --> 00:07:18.823
Yeah, you bet he did.

00:07:19.333 --> 00:07:21.281
Oh, hey, I tried to get
ahold of him, but I couldn't.

00:07:21.834 --> 00:07:22.809
How's he doing, anyway?

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:24.934
He's, um

00:07:25.523 --> 00:07:26.852
Wrapped up in a job right now.

00:07:27.117 --> 00:07:28.645
Well, we're missing the old man.

00:07:28.911 --> 00:07:29.863
We get sam.

00:07:30.018 --> 00:07:31.191
Even trade, huh?

00:07:31.723 --> 00:07:33.184
No, not by a long shot.

00:07:33.804 --> 00:07:35.464
I got something I want you guys to hear.

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.430
I listened to this.

00:07:38.939 --> 00:07:39.426
Well,

00:07:39.669 --> 00:07:41.153
It sounded like it was up your alley

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:43.389
Normally I wouldn't have access to this.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:47.237
It's the cockpit voice recorder
for united britannia flight 2485.

00:07:47.525 --> 00:07:48.433
It was one of ours.

00:07:48.956 --> 00:07:49.405
Mayday

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:12.721
Took off from here,

00:08:13.283 --> 00:08:15.055
Crashed about 200 miles south.

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:17.445
Now, they're saying mechanical failure.

00:08:17.647 --> 00:08:19.990
Cabin depressurized
somehow. Nobody knows why.

00:08:20.348 --> 00:08:21.645
Over 100 people on board.

00:08:22.431 --> 00:08:23.583
Only seven got out alive.

00:08:24.556 --> 00:08:25.337
Pilot was one.

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:27.880
His name is chuck lambert.
He's a good friend of mine.

00:08:28.462 --> 00:08:29.429
Chuck is, uh...

00:08:31.089 --> 00:08:32.387
Well, he's pretty broken up about it,

00:08:33.208 --> 00:08:34.081
Like it was his fault.

00:08:34.916 --> 00:08:35.723
You don't think it was?

00:08:36.266 --> 00:08:37.114
No, I don't.

00:08:37.834 --> 00:08:38.310
Jerry,

00:08:38.496 --> 00:08:40.336
We're gonna need passenger manifests,

00:08:40.421 --> 00:08:41.890
Hum...a list of survivors.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:42.407
All right.

00:08:42.526 --> 00:08:43.161
And huh...

00:08:43.241 --> 00:08:44.777
Any way we can take a
look at the wreckage?

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:46.690
The other stuff is no problem,

00:08:46.743 --> 00:08:47.564
But the wreckage

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:51.303
Fellas, the ntsb has it locked
down in an evidence warehouse.

00:08:52.282 --> 00:08:53.792
No way I've got that kind of clearance.

00:08:56.358 --> 00:08:56.848
No problem.

00:09:02.286 --> 00:09:02.737
Hey

00:09:02.895 --> 00:09:03.359
Hi.

00:09:06.325 --> 00:09:07.331
You've been in there forever.

00:09:08.858 --> 00:09:09.891
You can't rush perfection.

00:09:10.632 --> 00:09:11.745
Homeland security?

00:09:12.923 --> 00:09:13.837
That's pretty illegal,

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:14.618
Even for us.

00:09:15.453 --> 00:09:15.956
Yeah, well,

00:09:15.995 --> 00:09:17.320
It's something new, you know?

00:09:17.333 --> 00:09:19.028
People haven't seen it a thousand times.

00:09:23.837 --> 00:09:24.760
All right, so, what do you got?

00:09:24.979 --> 00:09:25.621
Well,

00:09:25.636 --> 00:09:28.202
There's definitely E.V.P. On
the cockpit voice recorder.

00:09:28.312 --> 00:09:28.656
Yeah?

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:29.235
Listen.

00:09:36.912 --> 00:09:37.929
"No survivors"?

00:09:38.821 --> 00:09:39.551
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:39.561 --> 00:09:41.032
There were seven survivors.

00:09:41.622 --> 00:09:42.248
Got me.

00:09:44.496 --> 00:09:46.014
So, what are you
thinking? A haunted flight?

00:09:46.459 --> 00:09:48.087
There's a long history of spirits and

00:09:48.134 --> 00:09:50.138
Death omens on planes and ships,

00:09:50.185 --> 00:09:51.249
Like phantom travelers.

00:09:51.296 --> 00:09:51.703
Mm-Hmm

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.660
Or remember flight 401?

00:09:53.894 --> 00:09:54.348
Right

00:09:54.568 --> 00:09:55.335
The one that crashed,

00:09:55.382 --> 00:09:56.884
The airline salvaged
some of this parts,*

00:09:56.947 --> 00:09:58.027
Put it in other planes,

00:09:58.336 --> 00:10:00.574
Then the spirit of the pilot and
copilot haunted those flights.

00:10:00.637 --> 00:10:00.981
Right.

00:10:01.044 --> 00:10:01.529
Yep.

00:10:02.484 --> 00:10:03.705
Maybe we got a similar deal.

00:10:04.441 --> 00:10:06.820
All rigth so, survivors which
one do you want to talk to first?

00:10:06.873 --> 00:10:08.594
Third on the list Max Jaffey.

00:10:08.688 --> 00:10:09.267
Why him?

00:10:09.314 --> 00:10:10.520
For one, he's from around here.

00:10:10.572 --> 00:10:11.323
And two,

00:10:11.902 --> 00:10:13.280
If anyone saw anything weird.

00:10:13.921 --> 00:10:14.454
He did.

00:10:15.612 --> 00:10:16.473
What makes you say that?

00:10:16.817 --> 00:10:18.054
Well, I spoke to his mother,

00:10:18.859 --> 00:10:20.206
And she told me where to find him.

00:10:22.947 --> 00:10:23.870
I don't understand.

00:10:23.882 --> 00:10:25.829
I already spoke with homeland security.

00:10:26.181 --> 00:10:26.770
Right.

00:10:27.276 --> 00:10:28.808
Some new information has come up.

00:10:29.044 --> 00:10:30.964
So if you could just
answer a couple questions...

00:10:31.169 --> 00:10:32.516
Just before the plane went down,

00:10:33.207 --> 00:10:35.531
Did you notice anything unusual?

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:36.592
Like what?

00:10:37.384 --> 00:10:38.613
Strange lights,

00:10:39.287 --> 00:10:40.601
Weird noises, maybe...

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:41.708
Voices.

00:10:43.628 --> 00:10:44.436
No, nothing.

00:10:46.369 --> 00:10:47.211
Mr. Joffey

00:10:48.171 --> 00:10:48.643
Jaffey.

00:10:48.946 --> 00:10:49.451
Jaffey.

00:10:49.586 --> 00:10:50.731
You checked yourself in here,

00:10:50.849 --> 00:10:51.304
Right?

00:10:52.519 --> 00:10:53.315
Can I ask why?

00:10:53.812 --> 00:10:55.119
I was a little stressed.

00:10:55.139 --> 00:10:56.990
I survived a plane crash.

00:10:58.656 --> 00:10:59.233
And that's

00:10:59.333 --> 00:11:00.129
What terrified you?

00:11:00.169 --> 00:11:01.303
That's what you were afraid of?

00:11:01.402 --> 00:11:03.910
I... I don't want to
talk about this anymore.

00:11:04.089 --> 00:11:05.880
I think maybe you did
see something up there.

00:11:06.915 --> 00:11:07.910
We need to know what.

00:11:08.978 --> 00:11:09.456
No.

00:11:09.595 --> 00:11:10.670
No, I was...

00:11:10.809 --> 00:11:11.565
Delusional

00:11:12.344 --> 00:11:13.300
Seeing things.

00:11:14.605 --> 00:11:15.625
He was seeing things.

00:11:19.176 --> 00:11:19.771
It's okay.

00:11:21.237 --> 00:11:24.164
Then just tell us what you
thought you saw, please.

00:11:28.807 --> 00:11:29.538
There was...

00:11:29.777 --> 00:11:30.349
This...

00:11:30.698 --> 00:11:31.366
Man.

00:11:33.051 --> 00:11:33.941
And, uh,

00:11:34.036 --> 00:11:35.451
He had these...

00:11:36.547 --> 00:11:37.170
Eyes...

00:11:37.265 --> 00:11:38.012
These, uh...

00:11:40.087 --> 00:11:41.295
Black eyes.

00:11:43.107 --> 00:11:44.935
And I saw him

00:11:45.715 --> 00:11:47.877
I thought I saw him...

00:11:51.819 --> 00:11:52.423
What?

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:56.891
He opened the emergency exit.

00:11:59.086 --> 00:11:59.690
But that's...

00:11:59.738 --> 00:12:00.851
That's impossible,

00:12:01.264 --> 00:12:02.522
Right? I mean, I looked it up.

00:12:02.554 --> 00:12:03.444
There's something like

00:12:03.603 --> 00:12:05.700
Two tons of pressure on that door.

00:12:07.864 --> 00:12:08.436
Yeah...

00:12:09.342 --> 00:12:10.232
This man, huh...

00:12:10.312 --> 00:12:12.807
Did he seem to appear and disappear.

00:12:13.064 --> 00:12:15.448
Rapidly.It would look
something like a mirage.

00:12:17.233 --> 00:12:18.552
What are you, nuts?

00:12:20.793 --> 00:12:21.937
He was a passenger.

00:12:21.969 --> 00:12:23.876
He was sitting right in front of me.

00:12:30.985 --> 00:12:32.145
Say here we are

00:12:32.257 --> 00:12:34.402
George Phelps, seat 20c.

00:12:35.038 --> 00:12:35.547
Hmm.

00:12:36.502 --> 00:12:38.696
Man, I don't care how strong you are.

00:12:41.191 --> 00:12:43.225
Even yoked up on pcp or something,

00:12:43.609 --> 00:12:46.597
No way you can open up an
emergency door during a flight.

00:12:47.569 --> 00:12:48.586
Not if you're human.

00:12:49.937 --> 00:12:51.923
But maybe this guy
George was something else

00:12:52.254 --> 00:12:54.415
Some kind of creature,
maybe, in human form.

00:12:54.844 --> 00:12:56.624
Does that look like a
creature's lair to you?

00:13:05.256 --> 00:13:06.559
This is your late husband?

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:09.023
Yes, that was my george.

00:13:09.844 --> 00:13:10.941
And you said he was a...

00:13:11.799 --> 00:13:12.594
Dentist?

00:13:13.014 --> 00:13:13.597
Mm-Hmm.

00:13:14.874 --> 00:13:17.183
He was headed to a convention in Denver.

00:13:20.047 --> 00:13:22.094
Do you know that he
was petrified to fly?

00:13:25.757 --> 00:13:27.166
For him to go like that...

00:13:29.813 --> 00:13:31.053
How long were you married?

00:13:33.457 --> 00:13:34.659
13 years.

00:13:35.416 --> 00:13:36.618
In all that time,

00:13:38.214 --> 00:13:39.942
Did you ever notice anything...

00:13:40.336 --> 00:13:41.839
Strange about him,

00:13:42.364 --> 00:13:43.979
Anything out of the ordinary?

00:13:47.184 --> 00:13:47.879
Well...

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:52.182
Uh, he had acid reflux,

00:13:52.313 --> 00:13:53.383
If that's what you mean.

00:13:57.517 --> 00:13:58.702
I mean it goes without saying.

00:13:58.721 --> 00:14:00.135
It just doesn't make any sense.

00:14:00.537 --> 00:14:02.152
A middle-Aged dentist with an ulcer

00:14:02.171 --> 00:14:03.899
Is not exactly evil personified.

00:14:04.669 --> 00:14:06.810
You know what we need to do is
get inside that ntsb warehouse,

00:14:06.828 --> 00:14:08.312
Check out the wreckage.

00:14:10.154 --> 00:14:11.055
Okay.

00:14:11.299 --> 00:14:12.264
But if we're gonna go that route,

00:14:12.293 --> 00:14:13.138
We'd better look the part.

00:14:19.516 --> 00:14:21.753
I look like one of the blues brothers.

00:14:22.072 --> 00:14:22.898
No, you don't.

00:14:23.386 --> 00:14:24.607
You look more like a...

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:26.354
Seventh-Grader at his first dance.

00:14:29.194 --> 00:14:30.396
I hate this thing.

00:14:30.433 --> 00:14:30.865
Hey.

00:14:31.241 --> 00:14:32.950
You want into that warehouse or not?

00:15:16.944 --> 00:15:17.658
What is that?

00:15:18.822 --> 00:15:19.987
It's an E.M.F. Meter...

00:15:20.437 --> 00:15:22.146
Reads electromagnetic frequencies.

00:15:22.937 --> 00:15:24.791
Yeah, I know what an E.M.F. Meter is,

00:15:24.809 --> 00:15:27.251
But why does that one look
like a busted-Up walkman?

00:15:28.304 --> 00:15:29.506
That's what I made it out of.

00:15:30.257 --> 00:15:31.214
It's homemade.

00:15:33.318 --> 00:15:35.177
Yeah, I can see that.

00:16:01.719 --> 00:16:03.278
Check out emergency door handle.

00:16:08.933 --> 00:16:09.872
What is this stuff?

00:16:10.003 --> 00:16:11.318
One way to find out.

00:16:24.181 --> 00:16:25.364
Homeland security?

00:16:26.197 --> 00:16:26.666
What?

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:28.206
One team of you guys isn't enough?

00:16:28.845 --> 00:16:29.690
What are you talking about?

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.039
Two of your buddies went
inside not five minutes ago.

00:17:12.427 --> 00:17:14.418
These monkey suits do come in handy.

00:17:15.939 --> 00:17:16.709
Listen Chuck

00:17:16.878 --> 00:17:17.929
It's like getting back on a horse,

00:17:18.477 --> 00:17:19.960
Only in this case, a little twin engine.

00:17:20.279 --> 00:17:21.106
Not even a horse

00:17:21.256 --> 00:17:22.045
More like a pony.

00:17:23.061 --> 00:17:23.981
I'll be right there with you too.

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:25.990
Anytime you feel like you don't
want the wheel, I'll take over.

00:17:26.911 --> 00:17:27.718
Look, Chuck,

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:29.427
We don't have to do this today.

00:17:29.803 --> 00:17:30.610
I'm not trying to rush you.

00:17:31.532 --> 00:17:32.246
No, the...

00:17:33.354 --> 00:17:34.349
The waiting is worse.

00:17:36.828 --> 00:17:38.669
Okay, they're filling
up the tank. Then we go.

00:18:11.865 --> 00:18:12.428
Huh.

00:18:14.099 --> 00:18:15.545
This stuff is covered in sulfur.

00:18:15.827 --> 00:18:16.447
You're sure?

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:17.987
Take a look for yourself.

00:18:18.006 --> 00:18:19.376
"You effin' piece of..."

00:18:19.376 --> 00:18:20.710
If you fellows will excuse me,

00:18:20.747 --> 00:18:22.175
I have an idiot to fire.

00:18:29.103 --> 00:18:29.498
Hmm.

00:18:30.474 --> 00:18:33.254
Here is not too many things that
leave behind a sulfuric residue.

00:18:33.357 --> 00:18:34.333
Demonic possession?

00:18:34.878 --> 00:18:37.995
It would explain how a mortal man would have
the strength to open up an emergency hatch.

00:18:38.166 --> 00:18:39.574
If the guy was possessed,

00:18:39.818 --> 00:18:40.513
It's possible.

00:18:40.816 --> 00:18:43.201
This goes way beyond
floating over a bed or

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:44.102
Barfing pea soup.

00:18:44.159 --> 00:18:45.680
What mean it's one thing
to possess a person,

00:18:45.717 --> 00:18:47.652
But to use them to take
down an entire airplane?

00:18:47.783 --> 00:18:49.492
You ever heard of
something like this before?

00:18:49.682 --> 00:18:50.207
Never.

00:18:56.123 --> 00:18:56.799
I'm ready.

00:18:57.006 --> 00:18:57.832
Let's do this.

00:19:06.088 --> 00:19:06.895
How you feeling?

00:19:07.158 --> 00:19:07.966
I feel great.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.031
You'll be back flying
jumbos before you know it.

00:19:10.407 --> 00:19:11.252
I hope so.

00:19:14.972 --> 00:19:15.798
How long we been up?

00:19:16.362 --> 00:19:18.108
Huh... Almost 40 minutes.

00:19:18.465 --> 00:19:18.916
Wow.

00:19:19.273 --> 00:19:20.268
Time really does fly.

00:19:47.549 --> 00:19:48.169
So,

00:19:48.563 --> 00:19:50.666
Every religion in every world culture

00:19:50.723 --> 00:19:53.577
Has the concept of demons
and demonic possession, right?

00:19:53.926 --> 00:19:56.874
I mean christian, native
american, hindu. You name it.

00:19:56.968 --> 00:19:58.640
Yeah, but none of them
describe anything like this.

00:19:58.734 --> 00:19:59.860
Well, that's not exactly true.

00:19:59.898 --> 00:20:01.306
You see according to japanese beliefs,

00:20:01.344 --> 00:20:04.067
Certain demons are
behind certain disasters,

00:20:04.112 --> 00:20:04.976
Both natural

00:20:05.089 --> 00:20:05.953
And man-Made

00:20:06.009 --> 00:20:08.262
One causes earthquakes.
Another causes disease.

00:20:08.281 --> 00:20:09.840
And this one causes plane crashes?

00:20:14.107 --> 00:20:15.271
All right, so, what?

00:20:15.309 --> 00:20:17.337
We have a demonthat's
evolved with the times

00:20:17.375 --> 00:20:19.102
And found a way to
ratchet up the body count?

00:20:20.022 --> 00:20:20.606
Yeah.

00:20:21.752 --> 00:20:22.353
You know,

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:25.620
Who knows how many planes it's
brought down before this one?

00:20:30.526 --> 00:20:31.033
What?

00:20:32.591 --> 00:20:34.582
I don't know, man. This
isn't our normal gig.

00:20:35.145 --> 00:20:36.798
I mean, demons, they
don't want anything just

00:20:36.873 --> 00:20:38.751
Death and destructionfor its own sake.

00:20:39.746 --> 00:20:40.460
This is big.

00:20:41.889 --> 00:20:43.016
I wish dad was here.

00:20:44.087 --> 00:20:45.345
Yeah. Me too.

00:20:52.109 --> 00:20:52.484
Hello?

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:53.667
Dean it's Jerry

00:20:53.855 --> 00:20:54.569
Oh, hey, Jerry.

00:20:54.869 --> 00:20:55.827
My pilot friend...

00:20:57.818 --> 00:20:58.944
Chuck Lambert, is dead.

00:21:00.937 --> 00:21:01.425
Wha...

00:21:01.801 --> 00:21:02.946
Jerry, I'm sorry. What happened?

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:05.350
He and his buddy went
up in a small twin.

00:21:05.425 --> 00:21:06.439
About an hour ago.

00:21:07.078 --> 00:21:07.923
The plane went down.

00:21:08.299 --> 00:21:09.087
Where'd this happen?

00:21:09.407 --> 00:21:11.566
About 60 miles west
of here, near nazareth.

00:21:12.132 --> 00:21:13.578
I'll try to ignore the irony in that.

00:21:13.822 --> 00:21:14.385
I'm sorry?

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:15.137
Nothing.

00:21:15.869 --> 00:21:17.803
Jerry hang in there, all right?
We'll catch up with you soon.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:20.758
Another crash?

00:21:20.965 --> 00:21:21.490
Yeah.

00:21:21.866 --> 00:21:22.336
Let's go.

00:21:22.542 --> 00:21:23.087
Where?

00:21:23.782 --> 00:21:24.401
Nazareth.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:37.292
Sulfur?

00:21:39.998 --> 00:21:41.181
Well, that's great.

00:21:41.914 --> 00:21:44.674
All right, that's two plane
crashes involving Chuck Lambert.

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:46.778
This demon sounds likeit was after him.

00:21:47.184 --> 00:21:48.273
With all due respect to Chuck,

00:21:49.363 --> 00:21:51.466
If that's the case, that
would be the good news.

00:21:51.879 --> 00:21:52.686
What's the bad news?

00:21:52.874 --> 00:21:55.447
Chuck's plane went down
exactly 40 minutes into flight.

00:21:55.612 --> 00:21:56.495
And get this

00:21:56.645 --> 00:21:58.241
So did flight 2485.

00:21:58.542 --> 00:21:59.349
40 minutes?

00:21:59.762 --> 00:22:00.438
What does that mean?

00:22:01.021 --> 00:22:02.335
It's biblical numerology.

00:22:02.598 --> 00:22:04.589
You know Noah's ark,
it rained for 40days.

00:22:04.645 --> 00:22:05.622
The number means death.

00:22:06.018 --> 00:22:06.750
I went back,

00:22:06.825 --> 00:22:09.492
And there have been six plane
crashes over the last decade

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:12.309
That all went down
exactly 40 minutes in.

00:22:13.361 --> 00:22:14.243
Any survivors?

00:22:14.919 --> 00:22:15.389
No.

00:22:15.831 --> 00:22:16.356
Or not

00:22:16.432 --> 00:22:17.502
Until now,at least

00:22:17.521 --> 00:22:19.812
Not until flight 2485, for some reason.

00:22:20.863 --> 00:22:22.309
And the cockpit voice recorder

00:22:22.422 --> 00:22:23.680
Remember what the E.V.P. Said?

00:22:23.981 --> 00:22:24.845
"No survivors."

00:22:28.831 --> 00:22:30.202
It's going after all the survivors.

00:22:31.422 --> 00:22:32.512
Something finish the job.

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:36.927
Really?

00:22:37.546 --> 00:22:39.312
Well, thank you for taking our survey,

00:22:39.330 --> 00:22:40.645
And if you do plan to fly,

00:22:40.664 --> 00:22:43.518
Please don't forget your friendsat
united britannia airlines.

00:22:44.251 --> 00:22:44.720
Thanks.

00:22:45.171 --> 00:22:45.809
All right.

00:22:45.924 --> 00:22:48.572
That takes care of Blaines
Anderson and Dennis Holloway.

00:22:48.686 --> 00:22:50.057
They're not flying anytime soon.

00:22:50.114 --> 00:22:52.649
So our only wildcard is the
flight attendant amanda walker.

00:22:52.912 --> 00:22:53.437
Right

00:22:53.475 --> 00:22:55.578
Her sister Karen said her flight
leaves Indianapolis at 8:00.

00:22:55.616 --> 00:22:57.175
Yeah but it's her first
night backon the job.

00:22:57.212 --> 00:22:58.564
That sounds like just our luck.

00:22:58.883 --> 00:23:00.498
Dean, this is a 5-Hour drive made

00:23:00.629 --> 00:23:02.075
Even with you behind the wheel.

00:23:02.659 --> 00:23:04.224
Call amanda's cellphone again,

00:23:04.242 --> 00:23:05.566
See if we can't head
her off at the pass.

00:23:05.621 --> 00:23:06.982
I already left her three voice messages.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:09.087
She must have turned her cellphone off.

00:23:10.130 --> 00:23:11.882
God,we're never gonna make it.

00:23:11.938 --> 00:23:12.627
We'll make it.

00:23:26.962 --> 00:23:27.596
Right there.

00:23:27.708 --> 00:23:28.826
They're boarding in 30 minutes.

00:23:28.975 --> 00:23:29.552
Okay.

00:23:30.093 --> 00:23:31.453
We still have some cards to play.

00:23:31.504 --> 00:23:32.492
We need to find a phone.

00:23:35.675 --> 00:23:36.607
Airport Services.

00:23:36.718 --> 00:23:37.799
Hi. Gate 13.

00:23:37.869 --> 00:23:39.024
<i>Who are you calling, Sir</i>

00:23:39.136 --> 00:23:40.753
I'm trying to contact an Amanda Walker.

00:23:40.775 --> 00:23:42.668
She's a flight attendant
on flight, um...

00:23:42.811 --> 00:23:44.088
Flight 424.

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:45.255
<i>"Amanda walker,"</i>

00:23:45.519 --> 00:23:47.237
<i>"Amanda Walker, you have a phone call"</i>

00:23:47.325 --> 00:23:49.130
<i>"White courtesy phone, gate 13."</i>

00:23:52.069 --> 00:23:53.126
Come on.

00:23:54.733 --> 00:23:55.967
This is amanda walker.

00:23:56.341 --> 00:23:57.111
Miss walker.

00:23:57.552 --> 00:23:59.362
Hi, this is Dr. James Headfield

00:23:59.384 --> 00:24:01.564
From st. Francis memorial hospital.

00:24:01.894 --> 00:24:03.722
We have a Karen Walker here.

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:04.625
Why Karen?

00:24:04.669 --> 00:24:06.782
Nothing serious just
a minor car accident,

00:24:06.817 --> 00:24:08.336
But she was injured, so

00:24:08.468 --> 00:24:11.462
Wa-Wait, that's impossible. I
just got off the phone with her.

00:24:14.727 --> 00:24:15.344
You what?

00:24:15.432 --> 00:24:16.290
Five minutes ago.

00:24:16.334 --> 00:24:18.999
She's at her house,
cramming for a final.

00:24:19.021 --> 00:24:19.967
Who is this?

00:24:21.168 --> 00:24:22.181
Uh, well...

00:24:22.599 --> 00:24:23.700
There must be some mistake.

00:24:23.722 --> 00:24:25.748
And how would you even know I was here?

00:24:27.487 --> 00:24:29.094
Is this one of Vince's friends?

00:24:30.743 --> 00:24:31.822
Guilty as charged.

00:24:32.636 --> 00:24:34.706
Wow. This is unbelievable.

00:24:35.565 --> 00:24:37.194
He's really sorry.

00:24:37.833 --> 00:24:39.418
Well, you tell him to
mind his own business

00:24:39.462 --> 00:24:41.223
And stay out of my life, okay?

00:24:41.311 --> 00:24:42.233
Yes, but...

00:24:42.585 --> 00:24:44.258
He really needs to see you tonight,

00:24:44.589 --> 00:24:45.315
So

00:24:45.425 --> 00:24:46.901
No, I'm sorry. It's too late.

00:24:47.099 --> 00:24:48.134
Don't be like that.

00:24:48.598 --> 00:24:49.699
Come on. The guy's

00:24:49.854 --> 00:24:51.483
A mess. Really. It's pathetic.

00:24:52.826 --> 00:24:53.509
Really?

00:24:53.729 --> 00:24:54.477
Oh, yeah.

00:24:55.138 --> 00:24:56.657
Look, I've got to go. Um...

00:24:56.668 --> 00:24:58.760
Tell him to call me when I land.

00:24:58.914 --> 00:25:00.676
No, no. Wait, Amanda. Amanda!

00:25:07.392 --> 00:25:08.317
How are you?

00:25:09.726 --> 00:25:10.893
Hey, boss. Hey

00:25:18.870 --> 00:25:19.772
Damn it!

00:25:20.279 --> 00:25:21.358
So close.

00:25:23.868 --> 00:25:25.563
All right, it's time for plan "B."

00:25:26.037 --> 00:25:27.094
We're getting on that plane.

00:25:27.204 --> 00:25:28.877
Oh,oh,Now, just hold on a second.

00:25:28.976 --> 00:25:29.592
Dean,

00:25:29.725 --> 00:25:30.892
That plane is leaving

00:25:30.936 --> 00:25:32.455
With over 100 passengers on board,

00:25:32.477 --> 00:25:33.402
And if we're right,

00:25:34.041 --> 00:25:35.340
That plane is gonna crash.

00:25:35.494 --> 00:25:36.132
I know.

00:25:36.243 --> 00:25:36.815
Okay.

00:25:36.908 --> 00:25:39.594
We're getting on the plane, we need
to find that demon and exorcise it.

00:25:39.638 --> 00:25:41.774
I'll get the tickets. You get
whatever you can out of the trunk.

00:25:41.818 --> 00:25:43.007
Whatever that will make
it through the security.

00:25:43.073 --> 00:25:44.372
Meet me back here in five minutes.

00:25:46.376 --> 00:25:47.389
Are you okay?

00:25:49.756 --> 00:25:51.033
No, not really.

00:25:52.310 --> 00:25:53.455
What? What's wrong?

00:25:55.624 --> 00:25:57.650
Well, I kind of have
this problem with, uh...

00:25:59.785 --> 00:26:00.600
Flying?

00:26:01.019 --> 00:26:02.736
It's never really been
an issue until now.

00:26:03.078 --> 00:26:03.936
You're joking, right?

00:26:04.002 --> 00:26:05.147
Do I look like I'm joking?

00:26:06.931 --> 00:26:08.516
Why do you think I
drive everywhere, sam?

00:26:09.639 --> 00:26:11.423
All right. Uh, I'll go.

00:26:11.712 --> 00:26:12.108
What?

00:26:12.130 --> 00:26:13.165
I'll do this oneon my own.

00:26:13.716 --> 00:26:14.508
Are you, nuts?

00:26:15.059 --> 00:26:16.424
You said that the plane's gonna crash.

00:26:16.468 --> 00:26:18.472
Dean, we can do it together,
or I can do this for myself.

00:26:18.516 --> 00:26:20.387
I'm not seeing a third option, here.

00:26:21.158 --> 00:26:22.083
Come on!

00:26:23.779 --> 00:26:24.462
Really?

00:26:26.774 --> 00:26:27.632
Man...

00:26:40.556 --> 00:26:42.515
Just try to relax. Just try to shut up.

00:27:12.378 --> 00:27:13.347
You're humming Metallica?

00:27:13.369 --> 00:27:14.514
Calms me down.

00:27:16.672 --> 00:27:17.531
Look, man,

00:27:17.905 --> 00:27:19.028
I get you're nervous, all right?

00:27:19.050 --> 00:27:20.613
But you got to stay focused.

00:27:21.952 --> 00:27:22.459
Okay.

00:27:22.481 --> 00:27:23.383
I mean, we got

00:27:23.494 --> 00:27:26.334
32 minutes and counting
to track this thing down

00:27:26.378 --> 00:27:29.659
Or who Everit's possessing, anyway
and perform a full-On exorcism.

00:27:29.681 --> 00:27:31.860
On a crowded plane.That's gonna be easy.

00:27:31.949 --> 00:27:33.578
Take it one step at a time, all right?

00:27:35.292 --> 00:27:36.040
Now,

00:27:36.162 --> 00:27:38.187
Who is it possessing?

00:27:39.266 --> 00:27:40.520
It's usually gonna be somebody

00:27:40.521 --> 00:27:41.578
With some sort of weakness, you know,

00:27:41.600 --> 00:27:43.714
A chink in the armor that
the demon can worm through,

00:27:44.121 --> 00:27:46.895
Somebody with an addiction
or emotional distress.

00:27:48.976 --> 00:27:49.571
Well,

00:27:49.769 --> 00:27:51.530
This is Amanda's first
flight after the crash.

00:27:51.574 --> 00:27:53.182
If I were her, I'd be pretty messed up.

00:27:53.248 --> 00:27:53.952
Mm-Hmm.

00:27:55.824 --> 00:27:56.704
Excuse me.

00:27:57.230 --> 00:27:57.979
Are you Amanda?

00:27:58.133 --> 00:27:58.970
No, I'm not.

00:27:59.014 --> 00:28:00.841
Oh, my mistake.

00:28:06.765 --> 00:28:08.813
All right, well, that's got
to be amanda back there,so

00:28:09.606 --> 00:28:10.662
I'll go talk to her,

00:28:10.795 --> 00:28:12.842
And, uh, I'll get a
read on her mental state.

00:28:13.283 --> 00:28:14.582
What if she's already possessed?

00:28:15.927 --> 00:28:17.380
There's ways to test that.

00:28:19.582 --> 00:28:20.837
I brought holy water.

00:28:21.718 --> 00:28:23.457
No. I think we can go more subtle.

00:28:23.924 --> 00:28:26.104
If she's possessed, she'll
flinch at the name of god.

00:28:26.676 --> 00:28:27.623
Oh. Nice.

00:28:29.759 --> 00:28:30.441
Hey.

00:28:30.607 --> 00:28:31.289
What?

00:28:31.465 --> 00:28:32.346
Say it in latin.

00:28:32.632 --> 00:28:33.293
I know.

00:28:33.381 --> 00:28:33.953
Okay.

00:28:34.196 --> 00:28:34.834
Hey!

00:28:35.341 --> 00:28:36.155
What?!

00:28:36.464 --> 00:28:38.291
Uh, in latin, it's "Cristo."

00:28:38.401 --> 00:28:40.207
Dude, I know! I'm not an idiot!

00:28:53.082 --> 00:28:54.205
Hi. Hi.

00:28:55.262 --> 00:28:56.341
Can I help you with something?

00:28:56.429 --> 00:28:57.332
Oh, no.

00:28:57.376 --> 00:28:59.335
I'm just a bit of an uneasy flier.

00:28:59.700 --> 00:29:01.351
It makes me feel better to
walk around a little bit.

00:29:01.461 --> 00:29:03.399
Oh, it happens to the best of us.

00:29:04.147 --> 00:29:07.186
Of course, you being a stewardess,
I guess flying comes easy to you.

00:29:08.320 --> 00:29:09.509
You'd be surprised.

00:29:09.839 --> 00:29:11.776
Really? You're a nervous flier?

00:29:12.459 --> 00:29:14.110
Yeah, maybe a little bit.

00:29:15.453 --> 00:29:17.105
How is it that,being a stewardess,

00:29:17.446 --> 00:29:18.525
You're scared to fly?

00:29:19.647 --> 00:29:20.881
Kind of a long story.

00:29:22.014 --> 00:29:23.600
Right. I'm sorry for asking.

00:29:23.677 --> 00:29:24.481
It's okay.

00:29:25.835 --> 00:29:27.442
You ever consider other employment?

00:29:28.719 --> 00:29:29.534
No.

00:29:30.062 --> 00:29:31.714
Look, everybody's scared of something.

00:29:31.769 --> 00:29:33.156
I just, uh...

00:29:33.949 --> 00:29:35.908
I'm not gonna let it hold me back.

00:29:37.185 --> 00:29:37.912
Huh.

00:29:38.936 --> 00:29:39.574
So...

00:29:42.393 --> 00:29:43.185
Cristo.

00:29:44.484 --> 00:29:45.805
I'm sorry. Did you say something?

00:29:51.047 --> 00:29:51.905
Cristo?

00:29:53.072 --> 00:29:54.283
I-I didn't, I didn't

00:29:55.318 --> 00:29:56.595
Yeah, nothing. Never mind.

00:30:00.796 --> 00:30:01.655
Okay.

00:30:09.600 --> 00:30:12.462
All right, well, she's got to be the
most well-Adjusted person on the planet.

00:30:12.506 --> 00:30:13.563
You said "cristo"? Yeah.

00:30:13.607 --> 00:30:14.939
And? There's no demon in her.

00:30:14.961 --> 00:30:16.524
There's no demon getting in her.

00:30:16.590 --> 00:30:18.374
So, if it's on the
plane, it can be anyone...

00:30:18.506 --> 00:30:19.563
Anywhere.

00:30:20.356 --> 00:30:22.535
Come on! That can't be normal! Hey, hey,

00:30:22.613 --> 00:30:24.947
It's just a little turbulence.

00:30:25.277 --> 00:30:26.840
Sam, this plane is going to crash, okay?

00:30:26.885 --> 00:30:28.338
So quit treating me
like I'm friggin' fool.

00:30:28.426 --> 00:30:30.209
You need to calm down.
No, I'm sorry I can't.

00:30:30.253 --> 00:30:31.563
Yes, you can.

00:30:31.959 --> 00:30:34.888
Dude, Stow the touchy-Feely,
self-Help yoga crap.

00:30:34.932 --> 00:30:35.989
It's not helping. Listen,
if you're panicked,

00:30:36.033 --> 00:30:37.244
You're wide opento demonic possession,

00:30:37.266 --> 00:30:39.336
So you need to calm yourself down

00:30:39.446 --> 00:30:40.436
Right now.

00:30:49.401 --> 00:30:50.194
Good.

00:30:51.471 --> 00:30:52.219
Now,

00:30:52.825 --> 00:30:55.159
I found an exorcism in here
that I think is gonna work

00:30:55.754 --> 00:30:56.987
The ritual romano.

00:30:58.044 --> 00:30:58.924
What do we have to do?

00:30:59.387 --> 00:31:00.180
It's two parts.

00:31:00.224 --> 00:31:02.646
The first part expels the
demon from the victim's body.

00:31:02.801 --> 00:31:05.905
It makes it manifest, which
actually makes it more powerful.

00:31:06.180 --> 00:31:06.951
More powerful?

00:31:07.061 --> 00:31:07.963
Yeah. How?

00:31:08.646 --> 00:31:10.099
Well, it doesn't need to
possess someone anymore.

00:31:10.143 --> 00:31:11.971
It can just wreak havoc on its own.

00:31:12.235 --> 00:31:13.798
Oh. And why is that a good thing?

00:31:14.327 --> 00:31:16.308
Well, because the second part

00:31:17.189 --> 00:31:18.664
Sends the bastard back to hell

00:31:19.061 --> 00:31:20.228
Once and for all.

00:31:21.747 --> 00:31:23.442
First thing's first we got to find it.

00:32:00.991 --> 00:32:01.923
Ohh! Don't do that.

00:32:02.031 --> 00:32:02.833
Anything?

00:32:03.027 --> 00:32:04.890
No, nothing. How much time we got?

00:32:05.150 --> 00:32:06.038
15 minutes.

00:32:07.295 --> 00:32:08.616
Maybe we missed somebody.

00:32:09.374 --> 00:32:10.890
Maybe the thing's just not on the plane.

00:32:12.160 --> 00:32:13.113
You believe that?

00:32:13.871 --> 00:32:14.954
Well, I will if you will.

00:32:24.458 --> 00:32:25.433
What? What is it?

00:32:26.755 --> 00:32:27.469
Cristo.

00:32:42.616 --> 00:32:43.786
She's not gonna believe this.

00:32:43.937 --> 00:32:44.976
12 minutes, dude.

00:32:47.390 --> 00:32:48.235
Oh, hi.

00:32:48.991 --> 00:32:50.584
Flight's not too bumpy for you, I hope.

00:32:50.657 --> 00:32:52.830
Actually, that's kind of what
we need to talk to you about.

00:32:53.047 --> 00:32:54.930
Um, okay.What can I do for you?

00:32:55.413 --> 00:32:57.007
This is gonna sound nuts, but

00:32:57.371 --> 00:32:59.665
We just don't have time for the whole
"the true this out there" speech right now.

00:32:59.713 --> 00:33:01.862
Look, we know you were on flight 2485.

00:33:03.598 --> 00:33:04.540
Who are you guys?

00:33:04.660 --> 00:33:06.809
Now, we've spoken to
some other survivors.

00:33:06.930 --> 00:33:09.320
We know something brought down that
plane and it wasn't a mechanical failure.

00:33:09.393 --> 00:33:10.407
We need your help

00:33:10.479 --> 00:33:12.194
Because we need to stop
from happening again.

00:33:12.314 --> 00:33:13.216
Here. Now. I'm sorry

00:33:13.288 --> 00:33:16.138
Here. I-I'm very busy. Whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa. Wait a second.

00:33:16.210 --> 00:33:17.610
I'm not gonna hurt you, okay?

00:33:17.755 --> 00:33:19.131
But listen to me, huh...

00:33:19.252 --> 00:33:21.539
The pilot in 2485, Chuck Lambert.

00:33:21.660 --> 00:33:22.529
He's dead.

00:33:23.212 --> 00:33:24.250
Wait. What?

00:33:24.419 --> 00:33:25.626
What, Chuck is dead?

00:33:25.916 --> 00:33:27.461
He died in a plane crash.

00:33:27.606 --> 00:33:29.152
That's two plane crashes in two months.

00:33:29.176 --> 00:33:30.818
That doesn't strike you as strange?

00:33:31.566 --> 00:33:33.353
Look, there was
something wrong with 2485.

00:33:33.378 --> 00:33:34.703
Now maybe you're
sensitive maybe you didn't

00:33:34.728 --> 00:33:36.128
But there's something
wrong with this flight, too.

00:33:36.153 --> 00:33:37.803
Amanda,you have to believe us.

00:33:43.109 --> 00:33:44.034
On...

00:33:44.984 --> 00:33:46.709
On 2485,

00:33:46.759 --> 00:33:48.559
There was this man.

00:33:48.609 --> 00:33:50.734
He...had these eyes.

00:33:51.009 --> 00:33:52.662
Yes. That's exactly
what we're talking about.

00:33:52.684 --> 00:33:54.337
I don't understand what
are you asking me to do?

00:33:54.359 --> 00:33:56.148
Okay. The copilot, we need
you bring him back here.

00:33:56.193 --> 00:33:58.254
Why? What does he have
to do with anything?

00:33:58.321 --> 00:33:59.250
Don't have time to explain.

00:33:59.272 --> 00:34:00.699
We just need to talk to him. Okay?

00:34:00.812 --> 00:34:02.193
How am I supposed to go in the cockpit

00:34:02.238 --> 00:34:04.072
And get the copilot--
Do whatever it takes

00:34:04.117 --> 00:34:05.793
Tell him there's
something broken back here,

00:34:05.838 --> 00:34:07.219
Whatever will get him
out of that cockpit.

00:34:07.287 --> 00:34:08.713
Do you know that I could lose my job

00:34:08.736 --> 00:34:10.910
If you -- You're gonna lose a
lot more if you don't help us out.

00:34:17.508 --> 00:34:18.255
Okay.

00:34:58.334 --> 00:34:59.489
Yeah, what's the problem?

00:35:05.670 --> 00:35:08.341
Wait. What are you doing? You said
you were just gonna talk to him.

00:35:08.387 --> 00:35:09.858
We are gonna talk to him.

00:35:18.897 --> 00:35:20.218
Oh, my god.What's wrong with him?

00:35:20.284 --> 00:35:21.209
Look. We need you calm.

00:35:21.253 --> 00:35:23.037
We need you outside the curtain.
Well, I don't underst..., I don't know

00:35:23.081 --> 00:35:24.666
Don't let anybody in,
okay? Can you do that?

00:35:24.710 --> 00:35:25.987
Can you do that?

00:35:26.295 --> 00:35:26.880
Amanda?

00:35:27.123 --> 00:35:27.677
Okay.

00:35:28.407 --> 00:35:28.983
Okay.

00:35:30.661 --> 00:35:32.831
Hurry up, sam. I don't know
how much longer I can hold him.

00:35:54.748 --> 00:35:56.342
I know what happened to your girlfriend!

00:35:58.268 --> 00:35:59.818
She must have died screaming!

00:36:00.504 --> 00:36:02.142
Even now, she's burning!

00:36:05.051 --> 00:36:05.760
Sam!

00:36:09.365 --> 00:36:10.538
"Prayer"...

00:36:13.261 --> 00:36:13.970
I got him.

00:36:34.898 --> 00:36:35.518
Where'd he go?

00:36:35.585 --> 00:36:36.492
He's in the plane.

00:36:36.559 --> 00:36:38.064
Hurry up.We got to finish it.

00:38:25.395 --> 00:38:25.926
I don't know.

00:38:26.015 --> 00:38:27.233
I was walking through the airport,

00:38:27.476 --> 00:38:28.783
Then it all goes blank.

00:38:29.070 --> 00:38:31.240
I don't even remember
getting on the plane.

00:38:33.251 --> 00:38:34.402
Anything else?

00:38:34.779 --> 00:38:35.686
No, that's all.

00:38:39.468 --> 00:38:40.420
"Thank you"

00:38:46.818 --> 00:38:47.837
Let's get out of here.

00:38:50.781 --> 00:38:51.623
You okay?

00:38:53.327 --> 00:38:54.080
Dean,

00:38:56.050 --> 00:38:57.666
It knew about Jessica.

00:39:00.341 --> 00:39:02.710
Sam, these things,t-They read minds.

00:39:03.086 --> 00:39:03.817
They lie.

00:39:04.591 --> 00:39:05.809
All right?That's all it was.

00:39:07.492 --> 00:39:08.112
Yeah.

00:39:10.554 --> 00:39:11.329
Come on.

00:39:17.528 --> 00:39:19.870
Nobody knows what you
guys did, but i do.

00:39:21.287 --> 00:39:22.970
A lot of people could have been killed.

00:39:24.431 --> 00:39:25.777
Your dad's gonna be real proud.

00:39:26.308 --> 00:39:27.637
We'll see you around, Jerry.

00:39:30.869 --> 00:39:31.844
You know, Jerry.

00:39:32.176 --> 00:39:32.751
Yeah.

00:39:33.367 --> 00:39:35.980
I meant to ask you how did you
get my cellphone number, anyway?

00:39:36.024 --> 00:39:37.662
I've only had it for like six months.

00:39:37.928 --> 00:39:39.124
Your dad gave it to me.

00:39:39.766 --> 00:39:40.204
What?

00:39:40.249 --> 00:39:41.577
When did you talk to him?

00:39:41.754 --> 00:39:44.190
I mean, I didn't exactly talk to him,but

00:39:44.610 --> 00:39:47.267
I called his number. His voice
message said to give you a call.

00:39:49.211 --> 00:39:50.008
Thanks again, guys.

00:40:06.900 --> 00:40:08.384
This doesn't make any sense, man.

00:40:08.406 --> 00:40:10.554
I've called dad's number like 50 times.

00:40:10.577 --> 00:40:11.883
It's been out of service.

00:40:13.206 --> 00:40:14.402
This is John Winchester.

00:40:14.734 --> 00:40:16.040
I can't be reached.

00:40:16.049 --> 00:40:18.396
If this is an emergency,
call my son, Dean

00:40:19.348 --> 00:40:24.148

866-907-3235

00:40:25.144 --> 00:40:26.229
He'll can help.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.500
